# Force LF line endings for shell scripts (CRLF breaks shebang on Windows Git Bash)
*.sh text eol=lf

# Force LF for the documents the suite reads as text too (#31583 QA). Without this the
# command pages and README check out CRLF on Windows, and a phrase assertion that
# flattens newlines but not carriage returns goes red in a fresh checkout while staying
# green in CI, which covers ubuntu and macos only. The helpers strip CR as well now, so
# this is belt and braces rather than the only defence.
*.md text eol=lf
*.bats text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
